</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Task B Configuration.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We route pipeline stages to three models: DeepSeek-V3.2 for span extraction (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau{=}0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau{=}0.0</annotation></semantics></math>, up to 8 spans) and technical judging; GPT-4o for dual candidate generation (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{1}{=}0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{1}{=}0.0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{2}{=}0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{2}{=}0.1</annotation></semantics></math>); and GPT-4o-mini for the <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">User Satisfaction Judge</span> (60% invocation rate) and micro-adjustments (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau{=}0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau{=}0.1</annotation></semantics></math>). Target length is question-type dependent (App. <a href="#A3.SS5" title="C.5 Question-Type Classification ‣ Appendix C Task B: Generation Details ‣ AILS-NTUA at SemEval-2026 Task 8: Evaluating Multi-Turn RAG Conversations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>). Selection combines technical scores, user preference, and
extractiveness calibration (App. <a href="#A3.SS3" title="C.3 Selection Score Details ‣ Appendix C Task B: Generation Details ‣ AILS-NTUA at SemEval-2026 Task 8: Evaluating Multi-Turn RAG Conversations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Task C Configuration.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All three judges and the arbiter use GPT-4o (<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau{=}0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau{=}0.0</annotation></semantics></math>). Refusal responses are capped
at 25 words. Answerable turns reuse the full Task B pipeline
configuration.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation Metrics</h5>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For Task A, we report Recall@<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and nDCG@<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>
(<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{5,10\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{5,10\}</annotation></semantics></math>). For Tasks B and C, we use
three metrics from the MTRAG evaluation
framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Katsis et al. (2025)</a></cite>: <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RB}_{\text{alg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>RB</mtext><mtext>alg</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RB}_{\text{alg}}</annotation></semantics></math>
(reference-based algorithmic),
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RB}_{\text{llm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>RB</mtext><mtext>llm</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RB}_{\text{llm}}</annotation></semantics></math> (reference-based LLM judge),
and <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RL}_{\text{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>RL</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RL}_{\text{F}}</annotation></semantics></math> (reference-less
faithfulness). The official ranking metric is the
harmonic mean (HM) of these three scores.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Results and Analysis</h2>

<section id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Official Results.</h5>

<div id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ A.4 Official Test Set Results ‣ Appendix A Dataset Details ‣ AILS-NTUA at SemEval-2026 Task 8: Evaluating Multi-Turn RAG Conversations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> reports leaderboard performance.
Our system ranks first on Task A
(nDCG@5: 0.5776, <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>20.5% over the strongest baseline),
validating the single-retriever, multi-query hypothesis. On Task B we rank second (HM: 0.7698 vs. top: 0.7827),
with strong faithfulness (<math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RL}_{\text{F}}{=}0.8971" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>RL</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8971</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RL}_{\text{F}}{=}0.8971</annotation></semantics></math>) and LLM quality (<math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RB}_{\text{llm}}{=}0.8321" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>RB</mtext><mtext>llm</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8321</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RB}_{\text{llm}}{=}0.8321</annotation></semantics></math>), indicating effective grounding. The Task B<math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math>C gap
(0.7698<math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math>0.5409) reflects compounding retrieval errors,
most visibly in <math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RB}_{\text{alg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>RB</mtext><mtext>alg</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RB}_{\text{alg}}</annotation></semantics></math>
(0.6327<math id="S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math>0.3998).
Relative improvements between ablation variants remain
consistent across development and test splits, suggesting
that the ablation findings reported below generalize
beyond the development set.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S5.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
