<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Optimized individual retrievers.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure that ELSER’s advantage is not an artifact of pipeline
co-optimization, we also optimized each retriever independently
using the same downstream pipeline components (multi-strategy rewriting and
reranking), and then compared the resulting recall at multiple cutoffs
(Table <a href="#A2.T15" title="Table 15 ‣ Optimized individual retrievers. ‣ B.1 Retriever Comparison ‣ Appendix B Task A: Retrieval Details ‣ AILS-NTUA at SemEval-2026 Task 8: Evaluating Multi-Turn RAG Conversations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).
Even after optimization, ELSER maintains the best R@5/R@10, confirming that
its advantage is intrinsic rather than an artifact of score-scale
compatibility with downstream fusion.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_logical-block">
          
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
