<figure id="A2.T16" class="ltx_table ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 16: </span>Rewriting strategy comparison on the dev set.
<sup id="A2.T16.5" class="ltx_sup">∗</sup>Annotator prompt replicates the query rewriting prompt used during
MTRAG data collection <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Katsis et al. (2025)</a></cite> (see Appendix C.1 therein).
Non-LLM methods (FlanT5) fall below the unaugmented baseline,
confirming that rewriting <em id="A2.T16.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hurts</em> when not properly grounded.
Among LLM-based variants, Corpus-Specific achieves the best
single-strategy R@5 (<sup id="A2.T16.7" class="ltx_sup">†</sup>); the final pipeline uses five
complementary strategies (Minimal, Corpus-Specific, CoT, HyDE,
Anchor-Keyword). All LLM gains over the original query are
significant (<math id="A2.T16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{&lt;}0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{&lt;}0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, paired bootstrap).</figcaption>
</figure>
      
