<td id="A3.T33.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T33.2.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Routed (ours)</span></td>
<td id="A3.T33.2.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T33.2.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.743</span></td>
<td id="A3.T33.2.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T33.2.1.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.761</span></td>
<td id="A3.T33.2.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="A3.T33.2.1.5.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.726</span></td>
<td id="A3.T33.2.1.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.T33.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.0\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.0</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 33: </span>Uniform vs. routed model assignment (dev set). Routing
GPT-4o to generation only matches uniform GPT-4o quality at
one-third the cost. Relative cost normalized to our routed
configuration.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS6.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.6.2 </span>Number of Retrieved Passages</h4>

<div id="A3.SS6.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T34" title="Table 34 ‣ C.6.2 Number of Retrieved Passages ‣ C.6 Additional Generation Ablations ‣ Appendix C Task B: Generation Details ‣ AILS-NTUA at SemEval-2026 Task 8: Evaluating Multi-Turn RAG Conversations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a> varies the number of retrieved
passages provided to the generation pipeline. Using too few
passages (<math id="A3.SS6.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N{=}1</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A3.SS6.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>) limits evidence coverage, while too many
(<math id="A3.SS6.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N{=}7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N{=}7</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A3.SS6.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>) introduces noise from marginally relevant documents
that dilutes the extracted spans and increases hallucination. The
sweet spot lies at <math id="A3.SS6.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N{=}5</annotation></semantics></math>, which we adopt for Task B. Notably,
the finding that fewer passages can improve performance also
explains the <math id="A3.SS6.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>2.7 HM gain from reducing <math id="A3.SS6.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> from 5 to 3 in
Task C (Table <a href="#A4.T39" title="Table 39 ‣ D.3 Task C Ablation ‣ Appendix D Task C: Additional Analysis ‣ AILS-NTUA at SemEval-2026 Task 8: Evaluating Multi-Turn RAG Conversations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>), where retrieval noise
is amplified by the end-to-end setting.</p>
</div>
