<section id="A3.SS6.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.6.3 </span>Extractiveness Band Calibration</h4>

<div id="A3.SS6.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The extractiveness shaping function <math id="A3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(r_{4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(r_{4})</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#A3.E5" title="In Extractiveness shaping function. ‣ C.3 Selection Score Details ‣ Appendix C Task B: Generation Details ‣ AILS-NTUA at SemEval-2026 Task 8: Evaluating Multi-Turn RAG Conversations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>)
uses a target band of <math id="A3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.28,0.38]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.28</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.38</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.28,0.38]</annotation></semantics></math> as the ideal range. We arrived
at this band by analyzing dev set reference answers (mean 4-gram
overlap: 36.2%) and validating sensitivity to alternative bands.
Table <a href="#A3.T35" title="Table 35 ‣ C.6.3 Extractiveness Band Calibration ‣ C.6 Additional Generation Ablations ‣ Appendix C Task B: Generation Details ‣ AILS-NTUA at SemEval-2026 Task 8: Evaluating Multi-Turn RAG Conversations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a> shows that our chosen band
outperforms both tighter and looser alternatives: a tighter band
<math id="A3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.30,0.40]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.30</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.40</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.30,0.40]</annotation></semantics></math> over-penalizes valid responses that paraphrase more
heavily, while a looser band <math id="A3.SS6.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.20,0.50]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.20</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.50</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.20,0.50]</annotation></semantics></math> fails to distinguish
hallucination-prone outputs from well-grounded ones.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS6.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Theoretically, the optimal band corresponds to the region of the
extractiveness distribution where faithfulness and naturalness are
jointly maximized. As shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ C.6.3 Extractiveness Band Calibration ‣ C.6 Additional Generation Ablations ‣ Appendix C Task B: Generation Details ‣ AILS-NTUA at SemEval-2026 Task 8: Evaluating Multi-Turn RAG Conversations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, dev
set responses in the <math id="A3.SS6.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.28,0.38]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.28</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.38</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.28,0.38]</annotation></semantics></math> range lie near the Pareto
frontier of the <math id="A3.SS6.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RL}_{\text{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>RL</mtext><mtext>F</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RL}_{\text{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A3.SS6.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{RB}_{\text{llm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>RB</mtext><mtext>llm</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{RB}_{\text{llm}}</annotation></semantics></math>
space, confirming that the band captures a genuine quality plateau
rather than an artifact of threshold selection.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T35" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T35.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
